"## Challenge: Program Your Own Custom Track\\n",
"\\n",
"1. **Transcribe a Melody:** Pick a recognizable short melody (e.g., *Tetris*, *Mary Had a Little Lamb*, *Star Wars*, or a game theme) and overwrite `NOTES_3` and `TIMES_3` in `SYNTH_SEQUENCER.ino`.\\n",
"2. **Update Array Sizes:** Ensure the integer inside the square brackets `[N]` for both `NOTES_3` and `TIMES_3` matches the **exact number of elements** inside your curly braces `{...}`.\\n",
"3. **Enable Looping (Optional):** To make your sequence repeat continuously, set `sequence_looping_3 = true;`. **Important:** When looping is enabled, you must set the very first note in `NOTES_3` to `REST` and the very first duration in `TIMES_3` to `0` so the timer resets cleanly.\\n",
"4. **Swap the Oscillator Engine:** Open `internal.cpp` in your project folder. Comment out (`//`) the currently active oscillator line and uncomment one of the alternate oscillator types (e.g., Sawtooth or Square) to match your song's style.\\n",
"\\n",
"## Troubleshooting\\n",
"\\n",
"\* **Dynamic Memory Exceeds 100% Error:** The Seeeduino Nano has limited SRAM. If your custom song is too long and triggers a memory compilation error, shorten `NOTES_3` and `TIMES_3` to fewer notes.\\n",
"\* **Out-of-Sync Rhythm:** Double-check that every entry in `NOTES_3` has a matching time entry at the exact same index in `TIMES_3`.\\n",
"\\n",
